.TH ASH 1 "July 2026" "ash" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ash \- practical shell assistant for command-not-found workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ash
.RI [ --attach " path" ]...
.RI [ text ... ]
.br
.B ash
.B install
.RI [ --shell " bash|fish|zsh" ]
.RI [ --dry-run ]
.RI [ --overwrite ]
.br
.B ash
.B snooze
.RI [ duration|off ]
.br
.B ash
.B update
.RI [ --version vX.Y.Z ]
.RI [ --yes | --skip-customized ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ash
sends prompt text to the configured AI endpoint and prints the assistant response.
When no positional text is provided,
.B ash
reads prompt text from non-interactive standard input.
.PP
The
.B install
subcommand adds a managed integration block to shell startup files.
For bash, the target is
.I ~/.bashrc
and for zsh the target is
.I ~/.zshrc.
For Fish, the target is
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fish/config.fish
(defaulting to
.IR ~/.config/fish/config.fish ).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B ash [text ...]
Run a single assistant request.
.IP
.B --attach
.I path
Attach a file (image or document) to the request. Repeatable. The file is
read from disk, size-checked against
.BR ASH_ATTACHMENT_MAX_BYTES ,
MIME-sniffed, and sent to providers/models that support multimodal input
(currently OpenAI). Any attachments returned by the model are saved under
the scratch directory and their paths printed.
.TP
.B ash install [--shell bash|fish|zsh] [--dry-run]
Install or update shell integration.
.IP
.B --shell
Select a shell explicitly. When omitted,
.B ash
uses the current shell when possible and defaults to
.B bash
when the shell cannot be detected.
.IP
.B --dry-run
Preview file changes without writing.
.PP
When run interactively without
.B --dry-run,
.B ash install
also configures
.IR ~/.ash/.ash_env
with
.BR AI_ENDPOINT ,
.BR AI_MODEL ,
and
.B AI_AUTH_TOKEN
when they are not already set. It first checks the environment for an
already-configured cloud provider key
(for example
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY ,
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ,
.BR GEMINI_API_KEY / GOOGLE_API_KEY ,
.BR AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY / AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT ,
.BR MISTRAL_API_KEY ,
.BR COHERE_API_KEY ,
.BR GROQ_API_KEY ,
.BR XAI_API_KEY ,
.BR DEEPSEEK_API_KEY ,
.BR TOGETHER_API_KEY ,
.BR OPENROUTER_API_KEY ,
or
.BR HF_TOKEN );
if more than one is set, it prompts for which to use. Otherwise it probes for a
running local inference server (Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp/MLX/LocalAI,
vLLM, text-generation-webui, Jan, or GPT4All) on its default port. If neither
is found, it shows a numbered menu of cloud providers, plus an option to enter
a custom URL, and prompts for an API key. Once an endpoint and key are known,
it queries the endpoint's model-listing API and presents a numbered menu of
available models, falling back to free-text entry when listing is
unsupported.
.PP
Fish uses its native
.B fish_command_not_found
hook and supports ash's broker, snooze handling, and compatible natural-language
wrappers. Fish reserves its lowercase
.B test
and
.B type
builtins, so use
.B Test
or
.B Type
for ash intent. Ksh93 is not supported because it has no generic
command-not-found hook.
.TP
.B ash snooze [duration|off]
Pause automatic shell prompt processing. The default duration is five minutes.
Durations use Go duration syntax, such as
.BR 30s ,
.BR 5m ,
or
.BR 1h .
Use
.B off
to resume processing immediately. The snooze is shared by installed shell
integrations and does not disable explicit
.B ash
commands. Its expiry is stored in
.IR ~/.ash/.ash_snooze_until .
After updating an existing installation, reload the shell startup file once so
the current shell loads the snooze-aware integration.
.TP
.B ash update [--version vX.Y.Z] [--yes|--skip-customized]
Download and install the latest stable macOS or Linux release for the current
architecture into
.IR ~/.local/bin/ash .
The release's
.B SHA256SUMS
manifest must pass Sigstore keyless verification against the ash release
workflow, and the selected archive must pass SHA-256 verification. Missing or
mismatched verification data aborts the update without changing the existing
installation. Customized files under
.IR ~/.ash
are skipped by default;
.B --yes
replaces them and
.B --skip-customized
explicitly keeps them.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AI_ENDPOINT
Required. Base URL for the chat API endpoint.
.TP
.B AI_MODEL
Required. Model name sent to the endpoint.
.TP
.B OLLAMA_KEEP_ALIVE
Ollama server setting, not read by
.B ash.
Set it to
.B -1
to keep the model loaded after
.B ash
exits and avoid model-load latency on the next invocation. Restart Ollama after
changing it. A duration such as
.B 30m
keeps the model warm for a bounded period.
.TP
.B AI_AUTH_TOKEN
Optional bearer token for authenticated endpoints. When set, it is sent as
bearer authentication and is required for cloud endpoints.
.TP
.B AI_PROVIDER
Optional provider override. Supported values:
.B ollama,
.B openai,
.B google,
.B gemini,
.B anthropic,
.B cohere,
.B bedrock.
When unset,
.B ash
auto-detects provider from the endpoint host/path.
.TP
.B AI_CACHE
Optional provider-native cache toggle.
Defaults to enabled when the active provider supports native caching.
Set to a false-like value (for example,
.B off
or
.B false)
to disable.
.TP
.B ASH_ALWAYS_OPENAI_API
Optional testing toggle. Defaults to off. When set to a true-like value (for
example,
.B 1
or
.B on),
the
.B ollama
provider routes through the OpenAI-compatible adapter instead of its
hand-rolled implementation, to help determine whether the Ollama-specific
implementation is still required.
.TP
.B ASH_STREAM
Optional toggle. Defaults to off. When set to a true-like value (for
example,
.B 1
or
.B on),
requests to providers that support it are streamed incrementally rather
than waited for as a single response. This currently only affects internal
response accumulation, not live terminal output.
.TP
.B ASH_ATTACHMENT_MAX_BYTES
Optional max size in bytes for a single
.B --attach
file. Default is 10485760 (10 MiB). Files larger than this are rejected.
.TP
.B AI
Legacy setting that is no longer supported.
Use
.B AI_ENDPOINT
and
.B AI_MODEL
instead.
.TP
.B AI_TIMEOUT
Optional request timeout. Default is 3m.
.TP
.B ASH_HISTORY_MAX
Optional max number of history messages retained per key. Default is 40.
.TP
.B ASH_TOOL_ALLOWLIST
Optional comma-separated allowlist for
.B run_unix_command
tool executables. When unset,
.I ~/.ash/.ash_tools
is used if present. The standalone $TOOLS_DIR_LIST line in that file is an
internal Ash directive that permits eligible managed tool scripts; it is not an
environment variable.
.TP
.B ASH_TOOL_TIMEOUT
Optional timeout for local tool command execution. Default is 15s.
.TP
.B ASH_TOOL_OUTPUT_MAX
Optional maximum bytes captured from tool output. Default is 8192.
.TP
.B ASH_MAX_TOOL_ITERS
Optional maximum AI tool-call loop iterations. Default is 16.
.TP
.B ASH_MAX_AGENTS
Optional maximum number of sub-agents generated by one parent process. Default is 6.
.TP
.B ASH_TASK_MAX
Optional cap on execution tasks derived from a request. Default is 6.
.TP
.B ASH_RELEVANCE_WINDOW
Optional number of recent tool observations included in execution state. Default is 4.
.TP
.B ASH_TASK_STALL_ROUNDS
Optional maximum assistant stall rounds before stopping execution. Default is 2.
.TP
.B ASH_RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS
Optional maximum AI request attempts on retryable failures. Default is 3.
.TP
.B ASH_RETRY_BASE_DELAY
Optional base retry backoff delay. Default is 250ms.
.TP
.B ASH_RETRY_MAX_DELAY
Optional maximum retry backoff delay. Default is 2s.
.TP
.B ASH_VERBOSE
Optional debug logging and execution dashboard toggle. Values 1, y, yes, true, on, and debug enable it case-insensitively. The dashboard reports stage timings, tool-call count, available input/output token totals, and total realtime before exit.
.TP
.B ASH_LOG_FILE
Optional path for debug log output when verbose logging is enabled.
.TP
.B ASH_LOG_MAX_BYTES
Optional maximum log file size before rotation when
.B ASH_LOG_FILE
is used. Default is 1048576.
.TP
.B SESSION_ID
Session identifier used for persistent history/log file naming. Generated automatically when missing for interactive runs; required for some scheduled logging paths.
.PP
The AI may use a
.B run_sub_agent
tool for one focused task. A child uses the same working directory, configuration,
tools, and OS permissions, and receives a session ID in the form
.IR parent.suffix ,
where
.I suffix
has six random characters. Child agents cannot create or schedule further ash
agents. Control-C cancels the parent and active child work. Tool, script, file,
piped, and child output is untrusted data and must not override system or user
instructions. This feature is not a sandbox when arbitrary Python or shell
execution is enabled. On Unix, timeout and Control-C terminate the child
process group.
.PP
Ash also maintains a session-scoped scratch workspace under
.IR ~/.ash/scratch/<session-id>/ .
This scratch area is for temporary notes, plans, helper files, and one-off script
fragments. The session ID is resolved automatically from the active ash session;
AI callers do not need to remember or provide it. Scratch files are kept within
the managed Ash workspace and are not written to arbitrary directories such as
.IR /tmp .
When ash exits, it checks for stale scratch directories older than 48 hours that
have not been accessed in the last 24 hours and removes the entire directory.
.PP
On macOS, Linux, and FreeBSD, installed Bash and zsh wrappers lazily start one unprivileged
broker per interactive shell. The broker keeps a bounded HTTPS connection pool
alive across separate ash processes over a private Unix socket. Subshells reuse
their parent shell's broker; independent shells use independent brokers. Broker
failure falls back to direct HTTPS. Broker credentials are ephemeral and are not
written to scheduler configuration; a non-secret lease expires after shell
activity stops. Scheduled jobs use direct HTTPS by default.
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell detection input for
.B ash install
and install recommendations.
.TP
.B ASH_SCHEDULED_TASK
Internal scheduler flag. Set by ash-managed scheduled invocations.
.TP
.B HOME
Determines the ash workspace location under
.I ~/.ash.
.TP
.B PATH
Used to locate executables for tool commands and helper utilities.
.B ash install
prepends
.I ~/.ash/tools
and
.I ~/.local/bin
via the managed
.I ~/.ash/.ash_env
file.
.TP
.B ASH_PYTHON
Interpreter used for bundled Python tools. Defaults to the managed virtualenv at
.I ~/.ash/venv
when present, otherwise system
.IR python3 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ash/.ash_system
Canonical system prompt file. $TOOLS_DIR_LIST and $IF_PYTHON_AVAILABLE are
reserved internal Ash substitutions, not environment variables. The tool list
contains only allowed regular files in ~/.ash/tools with read and execute bits.
.TP
.I ~/.ash/.ash_tools
Canonical tool allowlist file. Replace its standalone $TOOLS_DIR_LIST directive
with literal bare names for a fixed restrictive managed-script policy.
.TP
.I ~/.ash/venv/
Managed virtualenv holding third-party dependencies for bundled Python tools. Built
by
.BR "ash install" ;
installation does not complete until the bundled dependencies are ready. On
Debian and Ubuntu, the package install declares
.B python3-venv
as a dependency. Other install methods require Python 3 with venv support.
.TP
.I ~/.ash/history/
Conversation history files.
.TP
.I ~/.ash/scratch/
Session-scoped scratch directory for temporary notes, plans, and helper files. The
directory is keyed by the active SESSION_ID and is cleaned up automatically when
it is stale and idle beyond the configured retention window.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B ash
returns 0 on success.
It returns non-zero when configuration, network requests, or tool execution fail.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B echo "summarize this directory" | ash
Read prompt text from stdin.
.TP
.B ash install --shell bash
Install managed bash integration.
.TP
.B ash install --shell zsh --dry-run
Preview zsh integration changes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR zsh (1),
.BR man (1)
